Two fresh lane runs:
  python3 tools/ladder/musl.py --evocc .build/frozen/366fd796/evocc-darwin \
    --jobs 4 --budget 8 --build .build/case/m1 --no-receipt
  .evidence/ladder/musl/20261013T135849Z (summary SHA256 4475cbf932b7f6fa...)
  .evidence/ladder/musl/20261013T143422Z (summary SHA256 a28e7a44b254bb47...)
Each GCC reference baseline has 13 failing cases, not 17: the case
environment runs the two atfork and the two daemon cases correctly. Each
EvoCC mixed library survives two complete replays with the same 13 cases and
no added failure. All six REPORT files of the two runs are identical except
for the crashing tls_get_new-dtv case, which prints 7 to 10 dlsym lines
before its segfault. The shared-loader supplement PASSES in both runs. The
second summary records 13 dispositions and an empty undispositioned list.
It labels the two strptime cases test-expectation; the lane now spells that
category test-defect. Nothing else in the table changed after that run.
tests/contracts/ladder-musl-receipt.json is unchanged.

Dispositions (category: reason; evidence):

api/main (1)
  musl defect: pinned include/unistd.h (SHA256 ab2782955f7f5cd2...) lacks
  _PC_TIMESTAMP_RESOLUTION and _SC_XOPEN_UUCP. The POSIX.1-2024 <unistd.h>
  lists both. api/unistd.c does not compile (lines 117 and 238), so main does
  not link. musl master has not changed include/unistd.h since 2024-05-07.
  Evidence: baseline REPORT; musl-reference-boundaries.out; the patched conf
  supplement links and runs the original api/main 12/12.

dlopen, tls_align, tls_align_dlopen, tls_init_dlopen, tls_get_new-dtv (5)
  environment limit: the static-only lane (--disable-shared, -static) has no
  dynamic loader: "Dynamic loading not supported", "attempted static link of
  dynamic object". Evidence: the genuine loader lane runs all five unchanged
  programs, 5/5 with the GCC reference libc.so and 5/5 with the EvoCC
  candidate libc.so, each as PT_INTERP; musl-shared-loader.out.

strptime, strptime-static (2)
  test defect: the two checks sit under the test's "Glibc" comment. They
  expect %s to set the date and %z to accept -06. POSIX.1-2024 leaves the
  effect of %s unspecified and gives %z as +hhmm or -hhmm. The pinned source
  parses %s without an effect (lines 133-139) and requires four %z digits
  (lines 199-208). Evidence: baseline REPORT; musl-reference-boundaries.out;
  the patched time extension passes 12 x 45/45 and 24/24 original entries.

strtold, strtold-static (2)
  musl defect: hexfloat keeps one hex digit too few for binary128, so both
  inputs round to ...1112. musl master fixes it in 50979c5bc89a (2026-05-21);
  its message names both inputs. Evidence: musl-hex-tail-reduction.out; the
  patched numerics pass 12 x 5920/5920 and 180/180 original entries.

wordexp, wordexp-static (2)
  musl defect and environment limit: the library leaks shell stderr, exposes
  its helper arguments, misparses WRDE_NOCMD input and ignores WRDE_UNDEF; the
  pinned dash 0.5.12 has no dollar-single-quotes. musl master now has three of
  the library fixes. Evidence: musl-patched-wordexp.out; the patched library
  passes 12 x 133/133 probe checks and 24/24 original entries.

powf (1)
  musl defect: upward powf(0x1.fffffep+127, 1) raises INEXACT|OVERFLOW for an
  exact result. It is the only counted line; the 79 X-prefixed lines are
  upstream expected failures. powf.c has not changed in musl master since
  2019. Evidence: musl-powf-rounding-reduction.out; patched numerics PASS.

daemon-failure, daemon-failure-static (2)
  environment limit: with stdout on a host virtiofs file, exit waits after
  descriptor exhaustion. The case wrapper spools only these two supervisors
  to guest-local storage. Evidence: both fresh baselines PASS;
  descriptor-exit-filesystem.out; controls below.

pthread_atfork-errno-clobber, pthread_atfork-errno-clobber-static (2)
  environment limit: RLIMIT_NPROC does not constrain uid 0. The wrapper runs
  only these two cases as uid/gid 65534. Evidence: both fresh baselines PASS;
  musl-reference-boundaries.out; controls below.

Compiler defect: none. The EvoCC mixed replays reproduce the reference
failing set exactly. Every patched supplement passes equally for GCC14,
Clang19 and EvoCC at O0 and O2 against both archives.

Environment controls, .evidence/ladder/musl-environment/20261013/:
The unchanged test objects are linked against the reference archive. Three
rounds; only the execution environment changes.
  atfork as uid 0 without the wrapper: 3/3 FAIL, "fork succeeded despite
  rlimit". Through the wrapper as uid 65534: 3/3 PASS.
  daemon with stdout on a host-mounted file: 3/3 time out at 5.0 s. With
  guest-local stdout: 3/3 PASS in about 0.19 s. Through the wrapper: 3/3
  PASS in about 0.2 s. The load average was 72 to 78, so these timeouts only
  corroborate the B08d6 reduction; they are not independent evidence.

